# Application

Product logic. Register everything in `DependencyInjection.AddApplication()`.

```text
Features/       vertical slices + Shared/; domain folders (Dbo/, Chat/, Workspace/)
AI/             ChatOrchestrator, Agents, Tools, Memory, Workflows
Models/         AI turn shapes, ChatMessageRoles
Utilities/      technical cross-cutting only (crypto) — not slice business logic
```

### Helpers vs Utilities

| | `{Slice}/Helpers.cs` or `Shared/Helpers.cs` | `Application/Utilities/` |
|---|---------------------------------------------|---------------------------|
| **What** | Slice or cross-slice **business** logic | **Technical** plumbing with no slice owner |
| **Examples** | `EmailSettingsMapping` in `Workspace/EmailAccounts/Helpers.cs`, inbox date parsing for AI tools | `CryptographyHelpers`, `Encrypt()` extensions |
| **Uses entities/DTOs?** | Yes — maps, presets, domain rules | No — algorithms, formats, extensions |
| **Promote** | Handler → slice `Helpers` → `Shared/Helpers` | Add here only when 2+ slices need same technical helper and it is not domain mapping |

**Decision tree:** “Does this belong to one slice’s domain?” → `{Slice}/Helpers.cs`. “Used across slices but still product logic?” → `Shared/Helpers.cs`. “Generic technical helper (crypto, parsing lib-style)?” → `Utilities/`. When unsure, start in handler private and promote.

`WebApp/Utilities/` is separate — UI/auth/cookies only; do not put Application business logic there.

## Features — vertical slices

| Folder | Namespace segment | Repository | Entity |
|--------|-------------------|------------|--------|
| `Dbo/Users/` | `Application.Features.Dbo.Users` | `UserRepository` | `Dbo.User` (sign-in, profile, password) |
| `Dbo/EmailProviders/` | `…Dbo.EmailProviders` | `EmailProviderRepository` | `Dbo.EmailProvider` — system templates (read-only) + per-user custom |
| `Chat/ChatThreads/` | `Application.Features.Chat.ChatThreads` | `ChatThreadRepository` | `Chat.ChatThread` |
| `Chat/ChatMessages/` | `…Chat.ChatMessages` | `ChatMessageRepository` | `Chat.ChatMessage` |
| `Workspace/EmailAccounts/` | `Application.Features.Workspace.EmailAccounts` | `EmailAccountRepository` | `Workspace.EmailAccount` |
| `Workspace/Contacts/` | `…Workspace.Contacts` | `ContactRepository` | `Workspace.Contact` |
| `Workspace/Tags/` | `…Workspace.Tags` | `TagRepository` | `Workspace.Tag` (+ `TagAssignment`) |
| `Workspace/Buckets/` | `…Workspace.Buckets` | `BucketRepository` | `Workspace.Bucket` (+ `BucketAssignment`) |
| `Shared/` | `Application.Features.Shared` | `SharedRepository` (cross-slice taxonomy), `Helpers.cs`, `DTOs.cs`, `Services.cs` | — |

Profile/password stay on `Dbo/Users/`. **Deferred — server-backed prefs:** no `UserSetting` table until prefs or user memory need persistence. Color theme (Settings → Appearance, navbar toggle) stays **device-local** via `localStorage` (`webAppTheme` in `webapp.js`); do not add server theme storage or Get/Save Appearance handlers until cross-device sync is an explicit product requirement.

**Workspace referables — display vs identifier:** all workspace ER rows share one pattern. **`alias`** is the per-user unique handle (slugified on save via `EntityAliasRules.SlugifyOptional`); AI refs use `EntityRefs.Format` (`contact:`, `mailbox:`, `tag:`, `bucket:`). Display fields are not unique. **Contact** — `firstName`/`lastName` + optional `email` (unique when set). **EmailAccount** — no separate display name; `alias` is the primary label; `emailAddress` unique per user. **Tag/Bucket** — `name` is display-only; `alias` is the identifier. Only `alias` (+ domain keys like email) get unique indexes — not display labels.

**`Dbo.EmailProvider` access:** `IsSystem = true`, `UserId = null` → global read-only templates (all users). `IsSystem = false`, `UserId` set → custom template owned by that user (create/update/delete). List/get/slug-resolve always scope to `UserId`: system rows + that user's custom rows. Slug unique among system rows; slug unique per user among custom rows. SQL `CK_EmailProvider_Ownership` enforces the system/custom ownership pairing.

C# folders and namespaces use **PascalCase** (`Chat/`, `Application.Features.Chat.*`). SQL scripts live under `Infrastructure/Database/{schema}/` (lowercase SQL schema names).

Each slice and `Shared/` use the **same file names** where needed: `DTOs.cs`, `Repository.cs`, `Helpers.cs`, `Services.cs`. **All DI** in **`Application/DependencyInjection.cs`**.

```text
Features/{Domain}/{Area}/     e.g. Dbo/Users, Chat/ChatThreads, Workspace/Contacts
  DTOs.cs
  Repository.cs
  Helpers.cs        when needed
  Services.cs       when needed (slice-local facades)
  Commands/
  Queries/

Features/Shared/
  DTOs.cs
  Repository.cs
  Helpers.cs        cross-slice logic / mapping
  Services.cs       cross-slice facades (UserMailboxService, …)
```

**Least scope first** — full escalation tables in `solution.mdc` (global). Application specifics below.

Mirror Infrastructure and **Slice ↔ Shared**: one `DTOs.cs`, one `Repository.cs`, one `Helpers.cs`, one `Services.cs` per folder — add only when needed. Multiple types live in each file. No one-off `EmailSettingsMapping.cs`-style files.

| File | `{Slice}/` | `Shared/` |
|------|------------|-----------|
| `DTOs.cs` | Slice read shapes | Cross-slice read shapes |
| `Repository.cs` | Promoted EF for slice | Cross-slice EF |
| `Helpers.cs` | Validation, normalization, non-DTO transforms | Cross-slice logic |
| `Services.cs` | Slice-local facades | Cross-slice facades (`UserMailboxService`) |

- Slice repos: `IDbContextFactory<AppDbContext>` in ctor; each method owns ctx → query/mutate → `SaveChanges`
- **Handlers never inject `IDbContextFactory`** — all EF in slice repos (or `SharedRepository`)
- **Reads** → slice DTOs via `{Dto}.FromEntity(entity)` or `{Dto}.FromEntities(entities)` on `DTOs.cs`
- **Writes** → repo methods; return DTOs or status tuples
- **Repo → repo:** slice repo calls another slice repo or `SharedRepository` when cross-slice; promote to `SharedRepository` when query spans multiple entity folders

### Escalation (logic + data access)

Promote **logic** and **data access** on separate tracks. Do not mix EF in `Helpers.cs` or slice mapping in `Repository.cs`.

#### Logic escalation

| Level | When | Where |
|-------|------|--------|
| **1 — Handler private** | One use case only | `#region # Private Helpers` on handler (static or instance) |
| **2 — Slice helpers** | 2+ handlers, or handler + repo/UI | `{Slice}/Helpers.cs` |
| **3 — Cross-slice** | Multiple slices | `Features/Shared/Helpers.cs` |

Start in the handler. Move to `{Slice}/Helpers.cs` when reused within the slice. Example: `Workspace/EmailAccounts/Helpers.cs` (`EmailSettingsMapping`, `EmailSettingsCatalog`).

#### Services escalation

| Level | When | Where |
|-------|------|--------|
| **1 — Handler private** | One use case only | Handler or private helper |
| **2 — Slice services** | Reused within slice | `{Slice}/Services.cs` |
| **3 — Shared services** | Cross-slice | `Features/Shared/Services.cs` |

`Helpers` = stateless mapping/logic. `Services` = injectable facades (repos, Infrastructure ports). Example: `UserMailboxService` in `Shared/Services.cs`.

#### Data access

**All EF in repos.** Handlers inject slice repos only; never `IDbContextFactory`.

| Level | When | Where |
|-------|------|--------|
| **1 — Slice repo** | Default for all slice data access | `{Slice}/Repository.cs` — registered in DI |
| **2 — Shared repo** | Cross-slice query (multiple entity folders) | `Features/Shared/Repository.cs` |
| **3 — Repo → repo** | One slice repo needs another slice’s data | Inject the other `{Slice}Repository` (e.g. `EmailAccounts` → `EmailProviderRepository`) |

Private `*Async(AppDbContext ctx, …)` helpers inside a repo method are fine — same unit of work, not handler-passed ctx.

**Features owns all EF.** `AI/` and `Features/Shared/Services.cs` use slice repos or `SharedRepository` — never `IDbContextFactory`.

| Consumer | Single-slice data | Cross-slice data |
|----------|-------------------|------------------|
| Feature handler | `{Slice}Repository` | `SharedRepository` or second slice repo |
| `AI/`, `Shared` services | `{Slice}Repository` | `SharedRepository` |

If a repo needs a capability on another slice, inject that slice’s repo. Promote to **`SharedRepository`** only when the query truly spans slices (e.g. taxonomy joins).

`SharedRepository` is not a dump of every query — only true cross-slice access.

### Models / DTOs

| Kind | Place |
|------|--------|
| Slice read shape | `Features/{Domain}/{Area}/DTOs.cs` — static `FromEntity` / `FromEntities`, `AsResponse<T>()` |
| Cross-slice read shape | `Features/Shared/DTOs.cs` |
| Use-case message | `{UseCase}Request` : `ICommand<>` / `IQuery<>` |
| Use-case result | `{UseCase}Response` (may extend slice DTO) |
| AI turn | `Models/AI.cs` |
| App constants | `Models/Constants.cs` (`ChatMessageRoles`) |
| `Result` / `ErrorCode` | `MediatR.Results` |

**Entity → DTO mapping:** always `{Dto}.FromEntity(...)` on the DTO class in `DTOs.cs`. Extra parameters (joined provider, taxonomy, etc.) go on `FromEntity` overloads — not `*Mapping.ToDto` in `Helpers.cs`. `Helpers.cs` keeps validation, normalization, and non-DTO transforms (e.g. `ToEmailSettings`, `ToSettingsDto`).

**Request parameters:** when a request includes ownership, put `UserId` first. Name entity ids descriptively (`ProviderId`, `TagId`, `ContactId`, `EmailAccountId`, `ThreadId`) — not bare `Id`. In **Chat**, use `ThreadId` everywhere (requests, DTOs, AI models) — not `ChatThreadId`; the entity/SQL column stays `ChatThreadId`.

**Repo method names:** no redundant entity prefix on `{Slice}Repository` (`UpdateProfileAsync`, not `UpdateUserProfileAsync`). Prefer one atomic repo method when a use case needs read-then-write on the same row.

**Naming:** keep `{UseCase}Request` / `{UseCase}Response` — not `SignInCommand`. CQRS kind = `Commands/` or `Queries/` folder + `ICommand` / `IQuery`.

**Query naming (app-wide):** name reads as the operation — no ambiguity between list vs single-get.
- `GetAll{Entity}By{Filter}` — collection (e.g. `GetAllTagsByUserId`, `GetAllChatMessagesByThreadId`)
- `Get{Entity}ById` — single row by primary id (+ `UserId` for ownership)
- `Get{Entity}For{Purpose}` — purpose-specific read when shape/consumer differs (e.g. future AI search)
- Commands: `{Verb}{Entity}[{Detail}]` — e.g. `CreateChatThread`, `SaveContact`, `SendChatMessage`
- Delete commands return `{UseCase}Response` (empty class when no payload) — `ICommand<{UseCase}Response>`, not bare `ICommand`

**Repo read methods** mirror the query verb where the repo owns that read: `GetAllTagsByUserIdAsync`, `GetContactByIdAsync`, `GetChatThreadByIdAsync`. Soft-delete / active filters stay inside the method — not in the name.

**Repo reads for AI only** (`Application/AI/`, `Memory/`): suffix `ForAI` on the method name — e.g. `GetRecentChatMessagesByThreadIdForAIAsync`, `GetChatMessageCountByThreadIdForAIAsync`, `GetAllChatMessagesBeyondRecentWindowByThreadIdForAIAsync`. Same `{GetAll|Get}{Entity}By{Filter}` verb pattern; `ForAI` marks consumers in the AI layer (not MediatR queries).

**FluentValidation ↔ SQL/EF lengths:** validator `MaximumLength` / `Length` upper bound must match EF `HasMaxLength` on the mapped column. Source of truth: `Infrastructure/Database/{schema}/Tables/*.sql` and `AppDbContext.OnModelCreating`.

Do **not** put use-case types or slice DTOs in Infrastructure or WebApp.

### Use-case file order

1. `{UseCase}Request`
2. `{UseCase}Response`
3. `{UseCase}RequestValidator`
4. `{UseCase}RequestHandler`

**References:** `Dbo/EmailProviders/Queries/GetAllEmailProvidersByUserId.cs`, `Dbo/Users/Commands/SignIn.cs`, `Chat/ChatMessages/Commands/SendChatMessage.cs`.

### Template — handler (repo only)

Inject slice repo(s). No `# Private Helpers` for data access.

```csharp
public sealed class SignInRequestHandler(UserRepository userRepo)
    : IRequestHandler<SignInRequest, SignInResponse>
{
    public async ValueTask<Result<SignInResponse>> HandleAsync(SignInRequest request, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)
    {
        var result = new Result<SignInResponse>();

        #region # Execute
        var session = await userRepo.FindSessionByEmailAndPasswordAsync(request.EmailId, request.Password, cancellationToken);
        #endregion

        #region # Handle Result
        if (session is null)
            result.Failure(ErrorCode.NotFound, "Invalid Credentials");
        else
            result.Success(session.AsResponse<SignInResponse>());
        #endregion

        return result;
    }
}
```

### Template — slice repo method

```csharp
public sealed class EmailProviderRepository(IDbContextFactory<AppDbContext> _dbContextFactory)
{
    public async Task<IReadOnlyList<EmailProviderDto>> ListAsync(CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)
    {
        await using var ctx = await _dbContextFactory.CreateDbContextAsync(cancellationToken);
        var rows = await ctx.EmailProviders
            .AsNoTracking()
            .Where(x => x.IsActive && !x.IsDeleted)
            .OrderBy(x => x.SortOrder)
            .ToListAsync(cancellationToken);
        return rows.ConvertAll(EmailProviderDto.FromEntity);
    }
}
```

### Data access outside Features

`AI/` and `Features/Shared/Services.cs` inject **slice repos** or **`SharedRepository`** — never `IDbContextFactory`. If a capability needs DB access that is not on a repo yet, add the method to the slice repo first.

| Component | Repos |
|-----------|-------|
| `ChatOrchestrator` | `ChatMessageRepository` (history) |
| `ThreadMemoryService` | `ChatThreadRepository`, `ChatMessageRepository` |
| `UserMailboxService` | `EmailAccountRepository` |

### Handler rules

1. `var result = new Result<T>();` first line
2. `result.Success` / `result.Failure` — instance only
3. `#region # Execute` + `#region # Handle Result` always
4. **No EF in handlers** — inject `{Slice}Repository` (and `SharedRepository` or second slice repo when needed)
5. `#region # Private Helpers` only for **non-DB** orchestration (not data access)

| Repo param | Name |
|------------|------|
| `UserRepository` | `userRepo` |
| `ChatThreadRepository` | `chatThreadRepo` |
| `ChatMessageRepository` | `chatMessageRepo` |
| `EmailAccountRepository` | `emailAccountRepo` |
| `ContactRepository` | `contactRepo` |
| `TagRepository` | `tagRepo` |
| `BucketRepository` | `bucketRepo` |
| `EmailProviderRepository` | `emailProviderRepo` |
| `SharedRepository` | `sharedRepo` |

Entry: `mediator.SendAsync(new SignInRequest(...))` — pipeline in `mediatr.mdc`.

